        rdfs:comment        "Field, William. <u>An Historical and Descriptive Account of the town and castle of Warwick and of the Neighbouring Spa of Leamington</u>. 1815 (republished 1969). pp. 192-93.\nSpicer, Charles William. <u>History of Warwick Castle</u>. 1844. pp. 31-32, ill.\nThornton, Peter. The royal state bed. <u>Connoisseur</u>. May-August 1977, vol. 175. 139 p.\nWood, Lucy, 'A Royal Relic: the State Bedroom Suite at Warwick Castle'. <i>Furniture History</i>, vol. XLVIII (2012), pp. 45-104.\nWestman, Annabel.  <u>Fringe, Frog and Tassel. The Art of the Trimmings Maker in Interior Decoration in Britain and Ireland</u> (London: Philip Wilson, 2019, ISBN 978 1 78130 075 6), pp. 84-85."@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d53707bb-056f-358f-b7e0-97f3c1900ba1> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Field, William. <u>An Historical and Descriptive Account of the town and castle of Warwick and of the Neighbouring Spa of Leamington</u>. 1815 (republished 1969). pp. 192-93.\nSpicer, Charles William. <u>History of Warwick Castle</u>. 1844. pp. 31-32, ill.\nThornton, Peter. The royal state bed. <u>Connoisseur</u>. May-August 1977, vol. 175. 139 p.\nWood, Lucy, 'A Royal Relic: the State Bedroom Suite at Warwick Castle'. <i>Furniture History</i>, vol. XLVIII (2012), pp. 45-104.\nWestman, Annabel.  <u>Fringe, Frog and Tassel. The Art of the Trimmings Maker in Interior Decoration in Britain and Ireland</u> (London: Philip Wilson, 2019, ISBN 978 1 78130 075 6), pp. 84-85."@en .
